ing his phone?**\n\n- In **Frame 1**, the phone is held **in his hand, angled downward**, and he is looking **directly at the screen** — not at the camera lens or mirror reflection. This is typical of someone **checking messages, reading content, or reviewing something** on their phone — not filming themselves.\n- There is **no evidence of a selfie-style grip** (phone held at arm’s length, facing himself) or **eye contact with the lens** that would suggest he’s vlogging *at this moment*.\n- In **Frame 2**, the phone is no longer visible — he has set it down or put it away to focus on his face.\n\n➡️ **Conclusion**: He is **not vlogging in these frames**. He is **using the phone as a personal device**, not as a recording tool for an audience.\n\n---\n\n**Final Summary:**\n\n> In these two frames, the man is **not speaking**, **not vlogging**, and **not addressing an audience**. He is **checking his phone** in Frame 1 and then **performing a skincare step** (dabbing his face) in Frame 2. His facial expression and body language are calm, focused, and task-oriented — consistent with someone going through a private morning routine, not performing for a camera. The phone is being used as a personal device, not as a recording tool. This suggests these frames capture a **quiet, non-performative moment** within a larger vlog, rather than the vlogging act itself.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-2 (2 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/1FsiZgGZU70/frames/frame_0012.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/1FsiZgGZU70/frames/frame_0013.jpg\nVLM Response: Based on the visual evidence in these two frames, here’s a detailed analysis:\n\n**1. Is the person speaking to the phone camera? Is he talking to himself without a phone?**\n\n- In **Frame 1**, the man is looking down at a smartphone held in his right hand. His mouth is closed, and his expression is neutral to focused — he appears to be reading or interacting with the phone screen, not spe